# Q1: console logs are mirrored to WandB; keep them local
src/part1/logs/*

# Q2: weights + token streams live on /scratch (see src/part2/config.yaml); console logs are mirrored to WandB
src/part2/logs/*
# Q3: PNG previews of the figures (PDFs are used in the report)
src/part3/assets/*.png
# Q1: full test translations (~8 MB per variant) are uploaded to each variant's HF repo;
# outputs/translation_samples.csv (small) stays in git
src/part1/outputs/translations_*.csv
# 5 MB commit cap: tokenizers (~2 MB each) are regenerable (`python -m src.partN.tokenizer`) and
# Q1's is also in every Q1 HF model repo
src/part1/tokenizer/tokenizer.json
src/part2/tokenizer/tokenizer.json
# Q1: per-step routing logs (~215 KB each) are mirrored to WandB; their one plot,
# assets/moe_aux_and_balance.png, stays in git
src/part1/outputs/train_routing_*.csv
# Redundant copies (the same content is already committed elsewhere):
# src/report.md is the source of report.pdf at the repo root
src/report.md
# HF links are listed in report.pdf and src/part1/report.md
src/part1/outputs/hf_links.md
# Q2 summary tables are repeated in src/part2/report.md and report.pdf
